    "readme_description": "Suppose you have `n` integers labeled `1` through `n`. A permutation of those `n` integers `perm` (**1-indexed**) is considered a **beautiful arrangement** if for every `i` (`1 <= i <= n`), **either** of the following is true:\n\n- `perm[i]` is divisible by `i`.\n- `i` is divisible by `perm[i]`.\n\nGiven an integer `n`, return *the **number** of the **beautiful arrangements** that you can construct*.",
    "_readme_examples": {
        "list": [
            {
                "content": "```\nInput: n = 2\nOutput: 2\nExplanation:\nThe first beautiful arrangement is [1,2]:\n    - perm[1] = 1 is divisible by i = 1\n    - perm[2] = 2 is divisible by i = 2\nThe second beautiful arrangement is [2,1]:\n    - perm[1] = 2 is divisible by i = 1\n    - i = 2 is divisible by perm[2] = 1\n```"
            },
            {
                "content": "```\nInput: n = 1\nOutput: 1\n```"
            }
        ]
    },
